The idea: use **nested loops** to compare every element of the first array with every element of the second array. This uses **O(1) extra space** (no hash sets, maps, or auxiliary arrays).

## Python Implementation

```python
def find_common_elements(arr1, arr2):
    n, m = len(arr1), len(arr2)

    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(m):
            if arr1[i] == arr2[j]:
                # Avoid printing the same common element twice
                already_printed = False
                for k in range(i):
                    if arr1[k] == arr1[i]:
                        already_printed = True
                        break
                if not already_printed:
                    print(arr1[i], end=" ")
                break  # move to next element of arr1


